      "ALLISON: See?\nJENNIFER: Go ahead -- throw yourself away on strangers. Bek! ; Treat her good or you'll get sued by a bald-headed lawyer.\nALLISON: Do you have any reasonable. listings -- -- Miss Logan?\nLOGAN: I'm afraid nothing on God's earth is reasonable anymore. But we'll try to find something inter- esting.",
      "LOGAN: Are you acquainted with our French Quarter, Miss Parker?\nALLISON: The usual tourist walkabouts. I've visited before.\nLOGAN: Well, if it's roots you're looking for, you'll certainly find them here. We've quite a colorful history.\nALLISON: It's not exactly roots I'm looking for. Is this it?",
      "LOGAN: The bathroom was redone last year. Allison crosses to stick her head into the open bathroom, turns back to draw open a heavy drape which exp…\nALLISON: It is nice.\nLOGAN: I'm glad. The apartment up there is vacant, so you'll find it's very quiet. They exit into corridor.",
      "ALLISON: Hello!\nGERDE: You are the new tenant? -\nALLISON: Her glance is taken now by an open door to a ground level apartment. Another woman stands there smiling -- indeed a smile, sweet and warm. H…\nGERDE: We heard the apartment was rented -~ we were not sure. Some friends are visiting in a few weeks. We thought they might take the place for a …",
      "GERDE: Sandra will take your things up. Give her your keys, then you can be comfortable.\nALLISON: No, I'll take them later. They won't melt.\nGERDE: Don't be foolish. Sandra loves to help, don't you, dear?\nALLISON: Well -- thank you -- Sandra."
    ]
